 Singapore to keep LNG/diesel flowing and to accelerate talks on a legally binding protocol under their FTA.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"98f153861a30\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Singapore\",\"sentence_key\":\"f688703883e8\",\"sentence_index\":13},{\"text\":\"Australia secured additional diesel shipments from Brunei and South Korea amid Middle East disruptions.\",\"subject\":\"diesel supplies\",\"value\":\"extra diesel from Brunei and South Korea\",\"time\":\"mid-April 2026\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST reported (Apr 16) that Australia secured additional diesel shipments from Brunei and South Korea to bolster supply; the matched ST article supports this claim.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"365c072787c1\",\"draft_sentence\":\"More on this topic\\nAustralia secures extra diesel from Brunei, South Korea to bolster war-hit supply\\nAustralia refinery fire worsens fuel supply crunch amid Iran war\\n“Our neighbours know that providing fuel and fertiliser to Australia helps put food on the table in this region,” he said.\",\"sentence_key\":\"d78e98439a5e\",\"sentence_index\":43},{\"text\":\"Malaysia’s Petronas promised to prioritise providing Australia with excess fuel after domestic needs are met.\",\"subject\":\"Petronas assurances\",\"value\":\"prioritise Australia for excess fuel\",\"time\":\"Apr 16, 2026\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.95,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"CNA and ST directly report Anwar saying Petronas would supply excess fuel to Australia once domestic requirements are met.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"4117ffe17690\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Mr Albanese’s latest stop was Malaysia on April 16, where he met his Malaysian counterpart Anwar Ibrahim, who promised that state-owned oil and gas company Petronas will look to provide Australia with any excess fuel supplies.\",\"sentence_key\":\"15a3bb5390e0\",\"sentence_index\":26},{\"text\":\"The visits were at least partly aimed at reassuring Australian domestic audiences about fuel and fertiliser supplies amid Middle East tensions.\",\"subject\":\"purpose of tour\",\"value\":\"reassure domestic audiences about supplies\",\"time\":\"April 2026\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST quotes experts and frames the \\\"diesel diplomacy\\\" tour as sending reassurance to Australians and calming panic buying concerns.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"ebfcb746fdff\",\"draft_sentence\":\"The trips are aimed at providing reassurance that Australia, which is heavily reliant on fuel and fertiliser imports, will have steady supplies as tensions in the Middle East continue.\",\"sentence_key\":\"3e9d228d8a28\",\"sentence_index\":3},{\"text\":\"Brunei agreed to consult and avoid unjustified import/export restrictions and supplies a notable share of Australia’s urea and diesel imports (roughly 11% urea, 9% diesel).\",\"subject\":\"Brunei commitments and supply shares\",\"value\":\"consult on disruptions; 11% urea, 9% diesel\",\"time\":\"Apr 15, 2026\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST reports the Brunei joint statement on consultations/avoiding unjustified restrictions and provides the percentage shares of Australia’s imports from Brunei.\",\"importance\":\"minor\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"fbf9a8f68578\",\"draft_sentence\":\"During his visit, Mr Albanese met Brunei’s leader, Sultan Hassanal Bolkiah, and they agreed to avoid unjustified import and export restrictions and to “consult each other on any disruptions”.\",\"sentence_key\":\"ed9191e392bf\",\"sentence_index\":56}],\"claim_summary\":{\"supported\":6,\"weak\":0,\"contradicted\":0,\"total\":6},\"matched_sources\":[{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Australian PM’s diesel diplomacy tour calms fears at home\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/asia/austra