ards legally binding protocol for essential supplies\",\"url\":\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/australia-albanese-lawrence-wong-energy-security-trade-6046816\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Independent CNA reporting that corroborates ST’s account of Singapore commitments and the framing of the visit as securing essential supplies.\",\"snippet\":\"(Apr 10, 2026) CNA coverage of Albanese’s Singapore visit: both leaders said they are accelerating talks on a protocol to protect energy and critical supplies, including LNG and diesel; established dialogues and an Energy Ministerial Dialogue.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"CNA\",\"title\":\"Malaysia\'s Petronas to supply excess fuel to Australia as leaders vow closer energy ties\",\"url\":\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/asia/malaysia-petronas-supply-excess-fuel-australia-energy-ties-6060246\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Directly supports the draft’s specific claim about Petronas assurances to Australia following the April 16 meeting.\",\"snippet\":\"(Apr 16, 2026) Reports Anwar’s statement that Petronas would prioritise providing Australia with excess fuel after domestic needs are met, and notes the bilateral push to bolster energy security amid Middle East disruptions.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"CNA\",\"title\":\"Australia, Malaysia pledge to strengthen energy security amid Middle East uncertainties\",\"url\":\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/watch/australia-malaysia-pledge-strengthen-energy-security-amid-middle-east-uncertainties-6061056\",\"match_type\":\"related\",\"relevance_note\":\"Multimedia report that relates to the same meetings and themes; corroborates the bilateral emphasis on energy/food interdependence though it is a video package rather than a long written feature.\",\"snippet\":\"Video/news package (Apr 16, 2026) summarising the Australia–Malaysia joint pledges on energy security, interdependence on fuel/fertiliser and Albanese’s