(225, 'Singapore Gaming Industry Expands with Esports Training Hub and Community Events', 'The Straits Times reported that Singapore has opened a centralised esports training centre to nurture local talent, while community gaming events such as Nintendo showcases and indie festivals are dra', 'According to The Straits Times, Singapore is strengthening its position as a regional gaming hub with the launch of a centralised esports training facility. The centre provides structured coaching, high‑end equipment, and international exposure opportunities for local athletes. Officials highlighted that the initiative is designed to professionalise esports in Singapore, creating pathways for players to compete globally while also supporting grassroots development.\r\n\r\nThe report also noted that community‑driven gaming events are flourishing. Nintendo’s recent showcases and indie developer festivals have attracted large crowds, reflecting the growing diversity of Singapore’s gaming culture. These events complement the professional esports push by engaging casual players and fostering a vibrant ecosystem that spans both competitive and recreational gaming.\r\n\r\nTogether, these developments underscore Singapore’s ambition to become a leading hub for digital entertainment in Asia. By investing in infrastructure for professional athletes and supporting community events, the country is positioning itself at the intersection of esports, gaming culture, and digital innovation.', NULL, 'da8a992809761cdb70c42b894a22d1dd992d88b5f9d69f812715a2ab7e92a78b', '{\"fingerprint\":\"da8a992809761cdb70c42b894a22d1dd992d88b5f9d69f812715a2ab7e92a78b\",\"trust_score\":75,\"passed\":true,\"publish_decision\":\"needs_review\",\"summary\":\"Only one trusted source strongly supports the draft, so confidence remains limited.\",\"verdict\":\"Needs Review. Do not publish yet. The draft needs manual revision or stronger evidence before it can move forward.\",\"metrics\":{\"factual_accuracy\":76,\"source_quality\":80,\"bias_detection\":80,\"logical_consistency\":70,\"completeness\":60},\"rubric_metrics\":{\"factual_accuracy\":34,\"source_quality\":20,\"bias_detection\":8,\"logical_consistency\":7,\"completeness\":6},\"source_url\":\"\",\"source_label\":\"Compared against 6 trusted CNA/ST sources.\",\"misinformation_highlights\":[],\"improvement_suggestions\":[\"Add an exact CNA or ST article URL in the Reference Link field so the checker has a strong evidence anchor.\",\"Add missing context such as who said what, when it happened, where it happened, and what was officially announced.\",\"Rewrite or attribute weakly supported claims such as: \\\"The centre provides structured coaching and international exposure opportunities for local athletes.\\\".\",\"Aim to lift the trust score to 81 or above by grounding each key sentence in an exact CNA or ST article and removing broad unsupported conclusions.\"],\"claims\":[{\"text\":\"Singapore has opened a centralised esports training facility (the EXP) at Kallang Wave Mall.\",\"subject\":\"Singapore\",\"value\":\"opened centralised esports training facility at Kallang Wave Mall\",\"time\":\"at opening reported by ST\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST articles directly report the opening of the E-sports Experience Centre (EXP) at Kallang Wave Mall.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"c339fb04c4a1\",\"draft_sentence\":\"According to The Straits Times, Singapore is strengthening its position as a regional gaming hub with the launch of a centralised esports training facility.\",\"sentence_key\":\"549b3b9760c7\",\"sentence_index\":0},{\"text\":\"The centre provides high-end equipment, pro-team rooms and a live-streaming-ready event space.\",\"subject\":\"the centre (EXP)\",\"value\":\"high-end equipment, pro-team rooms, live-streaming-ready event space\",\"time\":\"as described in ST coverage of the opening\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.85,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST snippets list pro-team rooms, live-streaming-ready event space and high-end equipment for the EXP.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"902c7bbfd15e\",\"draft_sentence\":\"The centre provides structured coaching, high‑end equipment, and international exposure opportunities for local athletes.\",\"sentence_key\":\"98e09b68eff7\",\"sentence_index\":1},{\"text\":\"Officials said the initiative is designed to professionalise esports in Singapore and create pathways for players to compete globally.\",\"subject\":\"Officials / government\",\"value\":\"professionalise esports, create pathways for global competition\",\"time\":\"at time of report\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.8,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST coverage notes government-level recognition and framing of the EXP as supporting professionalisation and infrastructure for esports.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"e0e67e6d6755\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Officials highlighted that the initiative is designed to professionalise esports in Singapore, creating pathways for players to compete globally while also supporting grassroots development.\",\"sentence_key\":\"649bdc5e2142\",\"sentence_index\":2},{\"text\":\"The centre provides structured coaching and international exposure opportunities for local athletes.\",\"subject\":\"the centre (EXP)\",\"value\":\"structured coaching and international exposure opportunities\",\"time\":\"as implied in the draft\",\"match_score\":0.2,\"confidence\":0.3,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST mentions professional facilities and team rooms but does not explicitly document structured coaching programs or international exposure opportunities in the provided snippets.\",\"importance\":\"minor\",\"status\":\"contradicted\",\"claim_key\":\"1abb3d994b90\",\"draft_sentence\":\"The centre provides structured coaching, high‑end equipment, and international exposure opportunities for local athletes.\",\"sentence_key\":\"98e09b68eff7\",\"sentence_index\":1},{\"text\":\"Community-driven gaming events, including indie festivals and conventions, are attracting large crowds and complementing professional esports development.\",\"subject\":\"community gaming events\",\"value\":\"attracting large crowds; complement professional esports\",\"time\":\"ongoing (events reported by ST)\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.85,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST articles on GameStart, Campus Game Fest and other community events support claims about thriving community events, indie showcases and significant attendance.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"e3ea62bcebb4\",\"draft_sentence\":\"The report also noted that community‑driven gaming events are flourishing.\",\"sentence_key\":\"5a6a6b13e3a2\",\"sentence_index\":3}],\"claim_summary\":{\"supported\":4,\"weak\":0,\"contradicted\":1,\"total\":5},\"matched_sources\":[{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Singapore\'s largest E-sports Experience Centre opens at Kallang Wave Mall\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/sport/singapores-largest-e-sports-experience-centre-opens-at-kallang-wave-mall\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Directly supports the draft’s claim that Singapore opened a centralised esports facility offering pro team rooms, event space and high-end equipment; article dates from the EXP opening coverage (facility at Kallang Wave Mall).\",\"snippet\":\"The largest E-sports Experience Centre (EXP) was opened at the Singapore Sports Hub... a 12,000 sq ft facility that houses an integrated live-streaming-ready e-sports event space, pro-esports team rooms, e-sports cafe, LAN gaming area and high-end equipment.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Largest E-sports Experience Centre here opens\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/sport/largest-e-sports-experience-centre-here-opens\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Same-event coverage corroborating details about the EXP and government-level recognition — supports professionalisation and infrastructure elements in the draft.\",\"snippet\":\"Reports the opening of the EXP at Kallang Wave Mall by Minister Edwin Tong; describes features such as pro-team rooms, live-streaming-ready event space and gaming equipment.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Game convention GameStart kicks off at Suntec City\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/tech/game-convention-gamestart-kicks-off-at-suntec-city\",\"match_type\":\"partial\",\"relevance_note\":\"Supports the draft’s assertion that community gaming conventions and indie showcases attract large crowds and contribute to Singapore’s gaming culture; not tied to the EXP facility claim.\",\"snippet\":\"Coverage of the GameStart convention at Suntec, noting large attendance, showcases by indie developers, cosplay, early access to games and esports match stages.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Fourth annual Campus Game Fest kicks off at ITE College Central\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/tech/games-apps/fourth-annual-campus-game-fest-kicks-off-at-ite-college-central\",\"match_type\":\"partial\",\"relevance_note\":\"Provides evidence of grassroots and community-driven gaming events that complement professional esports initiatives in Singapore.\",\"snippet\":\"Describes Campus Game Fest organised with Singapore CyberSports & Online Gaming Association and ITE, featuring tournaments, showcases by student developers and community engagement.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"E-sports: NTUC Club steps up community gaming outreach with eight-team invitational\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/sport/e-sports-ntuc-club-steps-up-community-gaming-outreach-with-eight-team-invitational\",\"match_type\":\"partial\",\"relevance_note\":\"Supports the draft’s claim about community-driven events and grassroots development; shows community organisations using esports for outreach.\",\"snippet\":\"Reports NTUC Club’s eight-team Mobile Legends invitational aimed at youth engagement and grassroots outreach, livestreamed to the public.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Singapore to host Asian edition of gaming festival gamescom\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/spore-to-host-asian-edition-of-gaming-festival\",\"match_type\":\"related\",\"relevance_note\":\"Related evidence of Singapore’s role as a regional gaming hub through hosting major international gaming festivals, reinforcing the draft’s broader point about Singapore’s ambition in digital entertainment.\",\"snippet\":\"Announces that Singapore will host the Asian edition of gamescom Asia — a major gaming festival including esports, industry conferences, and public exhibitions.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"}],\"why_not_perfect\":[\"Contradicted claim(s) still lowered the score.\",\"Source quality is not at the maximum, so the evidence could still be stronger or more directly corroborated.\",\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"Some wording is still interpretive or less neutral than ideal.\",\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\"],\"why_not_perfect_details\":[{\"message\":\"Source quality is not at the maximum, so the evidence could still be stronger or more directly corroborated.\",\"examples\":[{\"type\":\"source\",\"label\":\"Source example\",\"text\":\"Game convention GameStart kicks off at Suntec City\",\"reason\":\"ST - article - partial\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/tech/game-convention-gamestart-kicks-off-at-suntec-city\"},{\"type\":\"source\",\"label\":\"Source example\",\"text\":\"Fourth annual Campus Game Fest kicks off at ITE College Central\",\"reason\":\"ST - article - partial\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/tech/games-apps/fourth-annual-campus-game-fest-kicks-off-at-ite-college-central\"}]},{\"message\":\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"Some wording is still interpretive or less neutral than ideal.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\",\"examples\":[{\"type\":\"claim\",\"label\":\"Clarify this sentence\",\"text\":\"The centre provides structured coaching, high‑end equipment, and international exposure opportunities for local athletes.\",\"reason\":\"ST mentions professional facilities and team rooms but does not explicitly document structured coaching programs or international exposure opportunities in the provided snippets.\",\"highlight_key\":\"98e09b68eff7\",\"source\":\"ST\"}]},{\"message\":\"Not every important claim is fully or exactly confirmed by the matched CNA/ST sources.\",\"examples\":[{\"type\":\"claim\",\"label\":\"Not fully confirmed\",\"text\":\"The centre provides structured coaching, high‑end equipment, and international exposure opportunities for local athletes.\",\"reason\":\"ST mentions professional facilities and team rooms but does not explicitly document structured coaching programs or international exposure opportunities in the provided snippets.\",\"highlight_key\":\"98e09b68eff7\",\"source\":\"ST\"}]}]}', '2026-04-30 15:43:42', 70, 14, 75, 0, NULL, 0, '2026-04-20 02:23:33', '2026-04-19 10:23:33', '2026-04-30 16:45:58', 'pending', NULL, 0),
(227, 'Massage shops', 'Massage shops set for stricter rules; no rooms, partitions or cubicles in open-concept outlets', 'SINGAPORE - Mandatory licensing will be imposed on all massage establishments, with the police bringing an end to rooms, partitions and cubicles in open-concept outlets, which are supposed to operate in full view of the public.\r\n\r\nThe change comes in the wake of public unhappiness over the current system, with the Singapore Police Force (SPF) noting an increase in vice-related activities and infringement of conditions imposed on open-concept massage establishments.\r\n\r\nOpen-concept establishments have been exempt from licensing since 2018, but they are required to be registered with the police.\r\n\r\n\r\nWith the changes, slated to take effect by the second half of 2026, all massage establishments will be subject to the same “fit and proper” requirements, the police said in a statement.\r\n\r\nThis means open-concept massage establishments will no longer be exempt from licensing.\r\n\r\nAll massage establishments will be subject to more stringent licensing criteria, and will need to obtain the relevant approvals from the Housing Board or Urban Redevelopment Authority before setting up shop.\r\n\r\n\r\nOpen-concept establishments must comply with conditions, including the requirement to not have rooms, partitions or cubicles within the shop.', NULL, 'ffddb9655eb59272f59c0e7b764cc6b2f5637e7a2c4551668f81795c68f9e76e', '{\"fingerprint\":\"ffddb9655eb59272f59c0e7b764cc6b2f5637e7a2c4551668f81795c68f9e76e\",\"trust_score\":92,\"passed\":true,\"publish_decision\":\"auto_publish\",\"summary\":\"Both CNA and ST support the core story.\",\"verdict\":\"Reliable. Auto publish approved because the CNA/ST evidence is strong enough for direct publication.\",\"metrics\":{\"factual_accuracy\":93,\"source_quality\":100,\"bias_detection\":80,\"logical_consistency\":80,\"completeness\":70},\"rubric_metrics\":{\"factual_accuracy\":42,\"source_quality\":25,\"bias_detection\":8,\"logical_consistency\":8,\"completeness\":7},\"source_url\":\"\",\"source_label\":\"Compared against 2 trusted CNA/ST sources.\",\"misinformation_highlights\":[],\"improvement_suggestions\":[\"Add an exact CNA or ST article URL in the Reference Link field so the checker has a strong evidence anchor.\",\"Add missing context such as who said what, when it happened, where it happened, and what was officially announced.\"],\"claims\":[{\"text\":\"Mandatory licensing will be imposed on all massage establishments.\",\"subject\":\"massage establishments\",\"value\":\"mandatory licensing imposed on all\",\"time\":\"\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"Both CNA and ST explicitly report that open-concept exemptions will be removed and all massage establishments will require licences under the new framework.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"56eac3a94765\",\"draft_sentence\":\"SINGAPORE - Mandatory licensing will be imposed on all massage establishments, with the police bringing an end to rooms, partitions and cubicles in open-concept outlets, which are supposed to operate in full view of the public.\",\"sentence_key\":\"62046e3b8a36\",\"sentence_index\":0},{\"text\":\"The police are bringing an end to rooms, partitions and cubicles in open-concept outlets; they must operate in full view of the public.\",\"subject\":\"open-concept outlets\",\"value\":\"no rooms/partitions/cubicles; operate in full view\",\"time\":\"\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"Both sources state exemption conditions include no rooms/partitions/cubicles and open-concept must be in full view.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"2a0c5be4fb2e\",\"draft_sentence\":\"SINGAPORE - Mandatory licensing will be imposed on all massage establishments, with the police bringing an end to rooms, partitions and cubicles in open-concept outlets, which are supposed to operate in full view of the public.\",\"sentence_key\":\"62046e3b8a36\",\"sentence_index\":0},{\"text\":\"Open-concept establishments have been exempt from licensing since 2018 (but must be registered with the police).\",\"subject\":\"open-concept establishments\",\"value\":\"exempt from licensing since 2018; must register with police\",\"time\":\"since 2018\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"Both CNA and ST note the 2018 exemption and registration requirement.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"3fd6177ddaeb\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Open-concept establishments have been exempt from licensing since 2018, but they are required to be registered with the police.\",\"sentence_key\":\"fe404be4147b\",\"sentence_index\":2},{\"text\":\"The changes are slated to take effect in the second half of 2026, with open-concept establishments moved to a Category 3 licence and subject to \'fit and proper\' requirements.\",\"subject\":\"implementation and licensing category\",\"value\":\"effective second half of 2026; Category 3 licence; subject to fit and proper requirements\",\"time\":\"second half of 2026\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"CNA and ST report the second-half-2026 timeframe and new licensing (Category 3) with fit-and-proper standards.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"1edab28d4683\",\"draft_sentence\":\"With the changes, slated to take effect by the second half of 2026, all massage establishments will be subject to the same “fit and proper” requirements, the police said in a statement.\",\"sentence_key\":\"52239ec975e5\",\"sentence_index\":3},{\"text\":\"The change comes after the SPF noted an increase in vice-related activities and infringement of conditions imposed on open-concept massage establishments.\",\"subject\":\"reason for change\",\"value\":\"increase in vice-related activities and condition infringements\",\"time\":\"\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.8,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST\'s snippet states the move follows public unhappiness and SPF noting an increase in vice-related activities and infringements; CNA mentions tightening but places less emphasis on \'public unhappiness\'.\",\"importance\":\"minor\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"efc1263371b7\",\"draft_sentence\":\"The change comes in the wake of public unhappiness over the current system, with the Singapore Police Force (SPF) noting an increase in vice-related activities and infringement of conditions imposed on open-concept massage establishments.\",\"sentence_key\":\"73af5b48bf17\",\"sentence_index\":1},{\"text\":\"All massage establishments will need relevant approvals from the Housing Board or Urban Redevelopment Authority before setting up.\",\"subject\":\"new setup approvals\",\"value\":\"need approvals from HDB or URA before setting up\",\"time\":\"\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.75,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST notes more stringent licensing criteria and the need to obtain relevant approvals (HDB/URA) before opening; CNA focuses on licensing framework but ST provides this planning-approval detail.\",\"importance\":\"minor\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"7a0b327d0833\",\"draft_sentence\":\"All massage establishments will be subject to more stringent licensing criteria, and will need to obtain the relevant approvals from the Housing Board or Urban Redevelopment Authority before setting up shop.\",\"sentence_key\":\"791c459893f1\",\"sentence_index\":5}],\"claim_summary\":{\"supported\":6,\"weak\":0,\"contradicted\":0,\"total\":6},\"matched_sources\":[{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Massage shops set for stricter rules; no rooms, partitions or cubicles in open-concept outlets\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/courts-crime/police-tighten-rules-for-massage-establishments-amid-increase-in-vice-activities\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Direct match: article text closely matches the draft’s key claims (licensing removal of exemption for open-concept outlets, prohibition on rooms/partitions/cubicles, 2018 exemption, effective second half of 2026, ‘fit and proper’ requirements).\",\"snippet\":\"SINGAPORE - Mandatory licensing will be imposed on all massage establishments, with the police bringing an end to rooms, partitions and cubicles in open-concept outlets, which are supposed to operate in full view of the public. Open-concept establishments have been exempt from licensing since 2018, but they are required to be registered with the police. With the changes, slated to take effect by the second half of 2026, all massage establishments will be subject to the same “fit and proper” requirements, the police said in a statement.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"CNA\",\"title\":\"Open-concept massage parlours to require licences under new police rules\",\"url\":\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/spf-massage-establishment-license-regulatory-changes-6069916\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Direct match: CNA reports the same SPF announcement and details (removal of 2018 exemption, Category 3 licence, prohibition on rooms/partitions/cubicles, second-half-2026 implementation), supporting the draft’s core story.\",\"snippet\":\"SINGAPORE: The Singapore Police Force (SPF) will tighten regulations on massage businesses later this year... Under a new regulatory framework, open-concept massage establishments will no longer be exempt from licensing... Open-concept massage establishments have been exempt from licensing since 2018, and only have to comply with exemption conditions such as registering with the police and ensuring that there are no rooms, partitions or cubicles in their premises... Under the new rules, which will come into effect in the second half of 2026, the exemption will be removed and replaced by the new Category 3 licence.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"}],\"why_not_perfect\":[\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"Some wording is still interpretive or less neutral than ideal.\",\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\",\"Not every important claim is fully or exactly confirmed by the matched CNA/ST sources.\"],\"why_not_perfect_details\":[{\"message\":\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"Some wording is still interpretive or less neutral than ideal.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"Not every important claim is fully or exactly confirmed by the matched CNA/ST sources.\",\"examples\":[]}]}', '2026-04-23 07:14:49', 79, 14, 92, 0, NULL, 0, '2026-04-27 01:10:31', '2026-04-21 14:48:49', '2026-04-28 02:28:06', 'published', 'A category expert rejected this article during final verification. Please revise it and submit it again.', 0),
(228, 'Open-concept massage parlours to require licences under new police rules', 'Open-concept massage parlours to require licences under new police rules', 'IRAN WAR SINGAPORE: The Singapore Police Force (SPF) will tighten regulations on massage businesses later this year, it said on Tuesday (Apr 21).\r\n\r\nUnder a new regulatory framework, open-concept massage establishments will no longer be exempt from licensing, SPF said in a news release.\r\n\r\nADVERTISEMENT\r\n\r\nThe move comes after the police observed a rise in vice-related activities and infringements of exemption conditions in open-concept massage establishments (MEs), and amid a steady increase in public unhappiness because of the \"number of open-concept MEs and the social disamenities they create\", SPF said.\r\n\r\nMassage establishments are currently grouped into two licence categories.\r\n\r\n\r\nCategory 1 licences are granted to those that operate in HDB shop houses, shopping centres and hotels, while Category 2 licences are for shops located away from residential areas, schools and places of worship.\r\n\r\nADVERTISEMENT\r\n\r\nOpen-concept massage establishments have been exempt from licensing since 2018, and only have to comply with exemption conditions such as registering with the police and ensuring that there are no rooms, partitions or cubicles in their premises that would allow massage services to be administered in private.\r\n\r\nUnder the new rules, which will come into effect in the second half of 2026, the exemption will be removed and replaced by the new Category 3 licence.\r\n\r\nOpen-concept massage establishments under the new category will be subject to more stringent licensing, including the requirement to obtain the relevant land-use approval from the Housing and Development Board (HDB) or Urban Redevelopment Authority before the premises can be used as an open-concept massage establishment.\r\n\r\n\"Operators must also comply with licensing conditions, including the requirement not to set up rooms, partitions or cubicles within the ME,\" SPF said.\r\n\r\n\"Existing open-concept ME operators will be granted a grace period to apply for and obtain a licence, after the changes are implemented. During this grace period, existing operators may continue to operate their open-concept MEs,\" SPF added.\r\n\r\nADVERTISEMENT\r\n\r\nHDB will be working closely with SPF to clamp down on errant massage establishments, Minister for National Development Chee Hong Tat said.\r\n\r\n\"Errant operators will not be permitted to continue their illegal business activities in our neighbourhoods, regardless of whether they are operating out of HDB rental or sold shops,\" Mr Chee added. \r\n\r\n\"We will weed them out and not allow such undesirable activities to spread in our housing estates and affect the living environment for residents.\"\r\n\r\nRelated:\r\n\r\nIN FOCUS: Why illicit massage parlours, hard-selling beauty salons are hard to get rid of in HDB estates\r\nSPF also said it will make three other changes, which will apply to all categories of licencees.\r\n\r\nADVERTISEMENT\r\n\r\nEstablishments must prominently display an SPF-issued poster at their shopfront that states the operator\'s licence number and key licence conditions, and includes a web link for the public to report any breaches to the police.\r\n\r\nThe posters must be clearly visible to the public. Failure to display the poster will be an offence, SPF said.\r\n\r\nTo reduce administrative burden, SPF will also extend the licence tenures of compliant licencees for up to five years, compared to the current three years.\r\n\r\nNew Category 1 and 2 licensees will continue to be issued a one-year provisional licence before the operators are reassessed, depending on their compliance history.\r\n\r\nNew Category 3 licencees will be issued licences valid for up to three or five years from the outset, subject to the SPF\'s assessment.\r\n\r\nLastly, SPF will remove the need for establishments to seek its approval for employee uniforms and replace the requirement with \"clear standards on uniform decency\".', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 65, 3, 0, 0, 'uploads/articles/1776791540_Screenshot 2026-04-22 010926.png', 0, '2026-04-22 09:12:20', '2026-04-21 17:12:20', '2026-04-22 09:12:20', 'draft', NULL, 0),
