18.9% are redesigning roles and creating new AI-related jobs.\",\"subject\":\"MOM study outcomes\",\"value\":\"6.2% reduced headcount; 18.9% redesigning/creating AI-related jobs\",\"time\":\"unreleased MOM study (Jan–Mar 2026)\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"Both sources cite these specific percentages from the unreleased MOM study as reported by Dr Tan.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"7caf9ba5e883\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Citing results of the unreleased MOM study, he said that 6.2 per cent of companies reported that they had reduced headcount.\",\"sentence_key\":\"192832de05a7\",\"sentence_index\":52}],\"claim_summary\":{\"supported\":6,\"weak\":0,\"contradicted\":0,\"total\":6},\"matched_sources\":[{\"name\":\"CNA\",\"title\":\"New tripartite council on jobs to help workers, businesses make AI skills \'as pervasive as possible\' - CNA\",\"url\":\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/tripartite-jobs-council-ai-impact-work-industry-business-employment-ntuc-mom-snef-6089891\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Directly supports core claims in the draft: council formation, co-chairs, goals (upskilling, job redesign, enterprise transformation), survey statistic, subsidy/list of eligible AI tools and NTUC benefits.\",\"snippet\":\"Reports formation of the Tripartite Jobs Council (NTUC, MOM, SNEF), quotes Ng Chee Meng, Manpower Minister Tan See Leng and SNEF president Tan Hee Teck, lists focus areas (support AI adoption, broad/sectoral training, targeted transition support), cites survey of 2,560 companies (70% not adopted AI), and lists eligible AI tools and NTUC membership subsidies.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"New tripartite council to help workers keep jobs, companies transform amid AI disruption | The Straits Times\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/new-tripartite-council-to-maximise-job-security-help-firms-amid-ai-disruption/\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"This is the primary ST source for the submitted draft; it directly matches the draft\'s text, quotes, dates and programme details (AI training, tool subsidies, statistics).\",\"snippet\":\"ST article by Sarah Koh (Published Apr 30, 2026) describing the Tripartite Jobs Council comprising NTUC, MOM and SNEF, co-chaired by Tan See Leng, Ng Chee Meng and Tan Hee Teck; outlines objectives (coordinated enterprise support, broad/sectoral training, transition support), cites unreleased MOM survey (70% firms not adopted AI), plans for AI bilingual workers and tool subsidies.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"}],\"why_not_perfect\":[\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\",\"Not every important claim is fully or exactly confirmed by the matched CNA/ST sources.\"],\"why_not_perfect_details\":[{\"message\":\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"Not every important claim is fully or exactly confirmed by the matched CNA/ST sources.\",\"examples\":[]}]}', '2026-04-30 17:39:36', 68, 1, 100, 0, NULL, 0, '2026-04-30 17:39:48', '2026-04-30 17:39:22', '2026-04-30 17:39:48', 'published', NULL, 0);
