(244, 'New tripartite council to help workers keep jobs, companies transform amid AI disruption', 'New tripartite council to help workers keep jobs, companies transform amid AI disruption', '\\\r\n\r\nWhile AI offers productivity boostg.\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nNTUC members to get subsidies on 21 AI tools from May, part of efforts to equip workers\r\nManpower Minister Tan See Leng highlighted improvements in workers’ livelihoods, as real incomes for the median worker grew by 1.6 per cent per year over the past five years\r\nBusiness\r\n\r\nSingapore must equip workers for AI-driven future: MOM, NTUC, SNEF\r\nThe new rules are meant to give travellers greater convenience.\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nCross-border taxis  fortnight of May is forecast to be above average over most parts of the island.\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nThundery showers, warm weather expected in first half of May\r\nDuring the collaboration, officers raided 382 locations in Singapore, Hong Kong, Japan, Malaysia, South Korea, Thailand and Brunei.\r\nSingapore\r\nfoaindosand\r\nOver 400 arrested, investigated in multi-national operation against online child sexual exploitation\r\n(From left) Ms Siti Amirah Mohamed Asrori, Ms Annamalai Kokila Parvathi and Ms Mossammad Sobikun Nahar arriving at Supreme Court on April 30\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nJudge overturns acquittal of three women who organised procession outside Istana, each fined $3k\r\n\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nWhy young Singaporeans see having kids as a loss, instead of\r\n\r\n\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nNTUC members to get subsidies on 21 AI tools from May, part of efforts to equip workers\r\nManpower Minister Tan See Leng highlighted improvements in workers’ livelihoods, as real incomes for the median worker grew by 1.6 per cent per year over the past five years\r\nBusiness\r\n\r\nSingapore must equip workers for AI-driven future: MOM, NTUC, SNEF\r\nThe new rules are meant to give travellers greater convenience.\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nCross-border taxis can drop off passengers anywhere in S\'pore, parts of Johor from May 4\r\nThe total rainfall for the first fortnight of May is forecast to be above average over most parts of the island.\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nThundery showers, warm weather expected in first half of May\r\nDuring the collaboration, officers raided 382 locations in Singapore, Hong Kong, Japan, Malaysia, South Korea, Thailand and Brunei.\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nOver 400 arrested, investigated in multi-national operation against online child sexual exploitation\r\n(From left) Ms Siti Amirah Mohamed Asrori, Ms Annamalai Kokila Parvathi and Ms Mossammad Sobikun Nahar arriving at Supreme Court on April 30\r\nSingapore\r\n\r\nJudge overturns acquittal of three women who organised procession outside Istana, each fined $3k\r\n\r\nSingapore\r\nSINGAPORE – A new triparts and adopt new tools, amid a disruption driven by artificial intelligence.\r\n\r\nThe Tripartite Jobs Council will comprise workers trade union National Trades Union Congress (NTUC), the Ministry of Manpower (MOM), and employers trade union Singapore National Employers Federation (SNEF).\r\n\r\nWhile AI offers productivity boosts and new job opportunities, a major concern is the reshaping of skills as AI automates many job functions including writing and coding.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n“There are valid concerns about job security, the relevance of skills, worries about obsolescence, as well as the rapid, accelerating pace of change. These are real concerns, and we take them very seriously.”', 'https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/new-tripartite-council-to-maximise-job-security-help-firms-amid-ai-disruption?ref=top-story', '0fe6381ad3294492a0b1cd52056e758ab541ab7ffa0e4db30240126b3678021f', '{\"fingerprint\":\"0fe6381ad3294492a0b1cd52056e758ab541ab7ffa0e4db30240126b3678021f\",\"trust_score\":91,\"passed\":true,\"publish_decision\":\"auto_publish\",\"summary\":\"Both CNA and ST support the core story. The supplied reference URL appears to be a valid exact CNA/ST article link.\",\"verdict\":\"Reliable. Auto publish approved because the CNA/ST evidence is strong enough for direct publication.\",\"metrics\":{\"factual_accuracy\":93,\"source_quality\":100,\"bias_detection\":90,\"logical_consistency\":40,\"completeness\":60},\"rubric_metrics\":{\"factual_accuracy\":42,\"source_quality\":25,\"bias_detection\":9,\"logical_consistency\":4,\"completeness\":6},\"source_url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/new-tripartite-council-to-maximise-job-security-help-firms-amid-ai-disruption?ref=top-story\",\"source_label\":\"Compared against 4 trusted CNA/ST sources.\",\"misinformation_highlights\":[],\"improvement_suggestions\":[\"Add missing context such as who said what, when it happened, where it happened, and what was officially announced.\"],\"claims\":[{\"text\":\"A new tripartite Jobs Council (NTUC, MOM and SNEF) will be set up to help workers and businesses navigate AI disruption.\",\"subject\":\"Tripartite Jobs Council\",\"value\":\"Will be set up to help workers and businesses navigate AI disruption\",\"time\":\"\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"Directly reported by both CNA and ST as the central event.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"884d63a25c14\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Singapore must equip workers for AI-driven future: MOM, NTUC, SNEF\\nThe new rules are meant to give travellers greater convenience.\",\"sentence_key\":\"f2aa4169924e\",\"sentence_index\":2},{\"text\":\"NTUC members will receive subsidies of up to 50% on subscriptions to more than 20 popular AI tools starting in May.\",\"subject\":\"NTUC members\",\"value\":\"Up to 50% subsidies on 20+ AI tool subscriptions from May\",\"time\":\"Starting in May\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.9,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST article explicitly states subsidies up to 50% for NTUC members for 20+ AI tools beginning in May.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"155d7a70b316\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Starting in May, NTUC members will be able to receive up to 50 per cent off subscription costs for a suite of more than 20 eligible AI tools that can support tasks like content creation and writing, by tapping their Union Training Assistance Programme benefits.\",\"sentence_key\":\"c4d98c345fee\",\"sentence_index\":37},{\"text\":\"Plans are in the works to train some 100,000 \'AI bilingual\' workers by 2029.\",\"subject\":\"National training target\",\"value\":\"Train ~100,000 \'AI bilingual\' workers by 2029\",\"time\":\"By 2029\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.8,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST coverage on national AI training initiatives reports the 100,000 target; related to the council\'s remit.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"29f851dbdd5b\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Plans are also in the works to train some 100,000 “AI bilingual” workers by 2029, by equipping the workforce with AI know-how to solve problems and redesign work processes for more efficiency.\",\"sentence_key\":\"8cd95daf8d9e\",\"sentence_index\":33},{\"text\":\"An unreleased MOM survey (Jan–Mar) found that about 70% of 2,560 companies in Singapore have not adopted AI for work.\",\"subject\":\"MOM survey\",\"value\":\"~70% of 2,560 companies have not adopted AI\",\"time\":\"Survey conducted Jan–Mar\",\"match_score\":1,\"confidence\":0.85,\"source\":\"CNA\",\"reason\":\"CNA reports the MOM survey result and sample size as described.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"652ff914aba7\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Singapore\",\"sentence_key\":\"29d4fc924bcf\",\"sentence_index\":3},{\"text\":\"The council will focus on coordinated workforce transformation support, broad-based and sectoral training, targeted transition support for at-risk workers, and public awareness to drive training uptake.\",\"subject\":\"Council focus areas\",\"value\":\"Workforce transformation, training, transition support, public awareness\",\"time\":\"\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.8,\"source\":\"CNA+ST\",\"reason\":\"ST and CNA describe the council\'s planned focus areas; draft phrasing is a concise summary of those aims.\",\"importance\":\"core\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"375d0319a546\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Broad-based and sectoral training for workers, as well as targeted transition support for at-risk worker segments and occupations to facilitate timely transitions\",\"sentence_key\":\"3d2dadc89bdc\",\"sentence_index\":27},{\"text\":\"The Government announced an initiative to give Singaporeans who take selected SkillsFuture AI courses six months of free access to premium AI tools, with details to be released later in 2026.\",\"subject\":\"SkillsFuture initiative\",\"value\":\"Six months free access to premium AI tools for selected SkillsFuture AI courses; details in 2026\",\"time\":\"Details to be released later in 2026\",\"match_score\":0.85,\"confidence\":0.75,\"source\":\"ST\",\"reason\":\"ST reporting on government AI initiatives includes free access for selected SkillsFuture course takers; draft aligns with ST but some timing/wording is paraphrased.\",\"importance\":\"minor\",\"status\":\"supported\",\"claim_key\":\"c74f84ae619b\",\"draft_sentence\":\"Singapore\",\"sentence_key\":\"29d4fc924bcf\",\"sentence_index\":3}],\"claim_summary\":{\"supported\":6,\"weak\":0,\"contradicted\":0,\"total\":6},\"matched_sources\":[{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"New tripartite council to help workers keep jobs, companies transform amid AI disruption\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/new-tripartite-council-to-maximise-job-security-help-firms-amid-ai-disruption/\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Direct match to draft: same event, co-chairs, aims, and specific measures (training targets, NTUC subsidies, SkillsFuture initiatives) are described in this ST piece.\",\"snippet\":\"A new Tripartite Jobs Council (NTUC, MOM and SNEF) will be set up to upskill workers, help companies redesign jobs and adopt AI tools; plans cited include training 100,000 \\\"AI bilingual\\\" workers by 2029 and NTUC members receiving up to 50% off subscriptions to eligible AI tools from May.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"NTUC members to get subsidies on 21 AI tools from May, part of efforts to equip workers\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/ntuc-members-to-get-subsidies-for-subscriptions-to-popular-ai-tools-part-of-ongoing-efforts-to-equip/\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Directly supports the draft claim about NTUC members receiving subsidies for AI tool subscriptions beginning in May and the 50% figure.\",\"snippet\":\"Starting in May, subscriptions to more than 20 popular AI tools (including ChatGPT, Claude, GitHub Copilot and Midjourney) will be subsidised by up to 50% for NTUC members under the Union Training Assistance Programme, with caps on yearly amounts by age group.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Singapore to train 100,000 AI-savvy workers by 2029\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/politics/singapore-to-train-100000-ai-savvy-workers-by-2029\",\"match_type\":\"related\",\"relevance_note\":\"Closely related: provides background and detail on the 100,000 \'AI bilingual\' training plan referenced in the draft; complements the tripartite council story.\",\"snippet\":\"Announces the National AI Impact Programme (NAIIP) to train some 100,000 \'AI bilingual\' workers by 2029, uplift 10,000 enterprises, and expand tailored AI fluency programmes (e.g., for accountancy and legal professions).\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"CNA\",\"title\":\"New tripartite council on jobs to help workers, businesses make AI skills \'as pervasive as possible\'\",\"url\":\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/tripartite-jobs-council-ai-impact-work-industry-business-employment-ntuc-mom-snef-6089891\",\"match_type\":\"direct\",\"relevance_note\":\"Direct match and corroboration from CNA: confirms the council, tripartite co-chairs, the MOM survey statistic, and SME adoption concerns mentioned in the draft.\",\"snippet\":\"Reports the launch of a new council by NTUC with tripartite partners to support workers and businesses navigating AI, cites a MOM survey finding about ~70% of 2,560 companies not having adopted AI and notes SME challenges in adoption.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"}],\"why_not_perfect\":[\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"Some wording is still interpretive or less neutral than ideal.\",\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\",\"Not every important claim is fully or exactly confirmed by the matched CNA/ST sources.\"],\"why_not_perfect_details\":[{\"message\":\"Some context or reporting detail is still missing.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"Some wording is still interpretive or less neutral than ideal.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"The article can still be clearer in how it connects evidence to conclusions.\",\"examples\":[]},{\"message\":\"Not every important claim is fully or exactly confirmed by the matched CNA/ST sources.\",\"examples\":[]}]}', '2026-04-30 17:59:53', 76, 4, 40, 0, 'uploads/articles/1777542318_windoge 10.jpg', 0, '2026-04-30 17:45:18', '2026-04-30 17:45:18', '2026-04-30 17:59:53', 'draft', 'A category expert rejected this article during final verification. Please revise it and submit it again.', 0),
(245, 'PM Wong to speak at May Day Rally on helping workers adapt to evolving roles due to AI, new tech', 'SINGAPORE – More details on helping workers adapt to changing roles in the face of new technologies will be shared by Prime Minister Lawrence Wong during his May Day Rally speech on May 1.', 'SINGAPORE – More details on helping workers adapt to changing roles in the face of new technologies will be shared by Prime Minister Lawrence Wong during his May Day Rally speech on May 1.\r\n\r\nIn a post on social media platform X on April 30, PM Wong said: “With AI and new technologies, job roles will evolve. But one thing does not change: our commitment to support every worker – to adapt, upskill and move forward with confidence.”\r\n\r\nThe May Day Rally will start at 9.30am, with PM Wong slated to deliver the keynote speech.\r\n\r\nwoah this is crazy... is it that reliable news? this could be bullshit \r\n\r\nHe had, in February, unveiled a record $154.7 billion Budget which, among measures to support families and individuals, will also provide more support for firms to stay competitive and make a national push to tap the potential of artificial intelligence.\r\n\r\nDuring his Budget speech, Mr Wong devoted a section to new policies covering businesses, workers and students to harness AI as a strategic advantage.', 'https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/pm-wong-to-speak-at-may-day-rally-on-helping-workers-adapt-to-evolving-roles-due-to-ai-new-tech?ref=singapore', NULL, NULL, NULL, 80, 4, 70, 0, NULL, 0, '2026-04-30 18:07:22', '2026-04-30 18:04:16', '2026-04-30 18:07:22', 'published', NULL, 0);
