_type\":\"partial\",\"relevance_note\":\"Provides qualitative evidence similar to the draft\'s anecdotes (youth perspectives, trade-offs of being off social media, feelings of missing out), supporting several narrative elements of the draft.\",\"snippet\":\"Features interviews with teenagers, parents and experts about social media addiction and its impact on attention, self-esteem and emotional health; notes some teens feel \'left out\' if not on social media.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"CNA\",\"title\":\"S\'pore youth who spend over 3 hours on social media daily tend to report symptoms of depression, anxiety, stress: IMH study\",\"url\":\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/news/young-people-spend-more-3-hours-social-media-daily-depression-anxiety-stress-imh-study-4632251\",\"match_type\":\"partial\",\"relevance_note\":\"Reinforces the draft\'s claim about associations between heavy social-media use and mental-health symptoms among Singapore youths; useful as empirical context for parental decisions described in the draft.\",\"snippet\":\"About a third of young people reported severe or extremely severe symptoms of depression, anxiety or stress; links excessive social-media use and cyberbullying to higher likelihood of mental-health symptoms.\",\"source_type\":\"article\"},{\"name\":\"ST\",\"title\":\"Google starts rolling out age-verification safeguards for under-18s in Singapore\",\"url\":\"https://www.straitstimes.com/singapore/google-starts-rolling-out-age-verification-safeguards-for-under-18s-in-singapore/\",\"match_type\":\"related\",\"relevance_note\":\"Provides policy/tech context referenced in the draft’s \'More on this topic\' links (age-verification safeguards) and underscores the evolving environment around protecting minors online, though it does not document the personal anecdote.\",\"snippet\":\"Google rolled out measures in Singapore to verify users\' ages and enable default safeguards (SafeSearch, wellbeing tools) for those estimated to 